multi process / component architecture


- seeder: manually add url into db
- crawler: ask for url (urls) (from dispathcer) and fetch contet for the url, write raw content back to db
    - ue golang, for massive parallel http fetching.
- dispatcher: responsible for giving out unvisited urls when requested. responsible for balancing traffic to different sites based on ongoing work
    - may also implicitly act as a queueing system
- processor: responsible for processing raw content, extract urls, and add them to db. may use rust to implement.
- db: storage. may need a CRUD service on top.
    - sharding can happen here
- frontend: UI for displaying status, progress, etc.
